<div class="wrap page-head"><p class="kicker">Founder and chairman</p><h1>Jack Figel</h1><p class="lede">Reader, publisher, and for thirty years the organizer of the conversation between East and West that the official dialogues could not hold on their own.</p></div>
<section class="band" style="padding-top:1.5rem">
  <div class="wrap bio-grid">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="dropcap">Jack Figel founded the Orientale Lumen Conferences in Washington, DC, in 1997 and has chaired every one since. He is president of Eastern Christian Publications in Fairfax, Virginia, the national chairman of the Society of St. John Chrysostom in the United States, and founder and chairman of the Orientale Lumen Foundation, the nonprofit that grew out of both.</p>
      <p>The idea was simple and, at the time, unusual: put Eastern Orthodox, Eastern Catholic, and Roman Catholic Christians in one room for several days, let them hear the same lectures and attend each other's liturgies, and see what friendships form. The official Catholic-Orthodox dialogue meets behind closed doors; Orientale Lumen meets in public, with lay people and with the Eastern Catholics who are seldom represented anywhere else. Ecumenical Patriarch Bartholomew called it an effort that "may be grass roots" but is "at the same time rooted in heaven." Cardinal Kurt Koch, then president of the Pontifical Council for Promoting Christian Unity, sent a personal message to the 2019 conference.</p>
      <p>Jack has led the Foundation's pilgrims into private audiences with Pope Francis and with the Ecumenical Patriarch, taken three conferences to Constantinople at the Patriarch's invitation, including a day at the Halki Theological Academy, and represented the Foundation at the Vatican's 2017 conference on nuclear disarmament. In 2023 the National Council of Churches gave him the Miller Award for Excellence in Ecumenical Leadership. In July 2026, at the thirtieth conference, the Apostolic Nuncio presented him with the medal of Pope Leo XIV's first year, sent by the Pope himself.</p>
      <p>He is a tonsured Reader in the Byzantine Catholic Church and lives in Fairfax, Virginia.</p>
      <h2 id="speaking">Invitations</h2>
      <p>Jack speaks to parishes, seminaries, and ecumenical gatherings on the Eastern Churches, the Catholic-Orthodox dialogue, and how ordinary Christians can take part in it. <a class="textlink" href="/contact/">Write to the Foundation →</a></p>
